https://dati.terna.it/en/generation/statistical-data 91169 icity consumption (IMSER) International comparisons Generation Generation Statistical data Unavailability UP International comparisons Transmission Transmission REMIT Network Unavailability Market & Adequacy Market & Adequacy Transit limits between market zones Connections Econnextion Fees Download Center Ita | Eng Notifications Remove all No notification Hub Generation Statistical data Statistical data Electricity data is without doubt Terna's most important operational data asset, with statistical processing for the entire sector at the national level amongst its exclusive duties by law. Since 2000, cutting-edge tools have been used to collect the data recorded by around 5,600 operators, including producers and distributors , available to all stakeholders, including those without technical knowledge. Anyone interested in understanding how the energy consumption market has changed in Italy with industrial and economic evolution over the last twenty years or what progress has been made towards international decarbonisation goals – through fundamental parameters such as capacity and electricity production – will find charts and files in this section with all the data from 2000 , divided by category. How to consult and interact with the graphs For all graphs For all graphs To download the data Choose the graph you would like to download the data for and set the desired filters Click any point on the graph, and 2 icons will appear at the top right Place the mouse over to show the More options label Click on the dots to make the selection menu appear Select the command you want
